\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces  Same as Figure \ref  {frequency tracking before and after1}, but for a GW signal (orange curve) injected into real LIGO noise. The $60 \, {\rm  Hz}$ line is visible as a vertical yellow band in the left panel; it cannot be discerned in the right panel. The signal recovered by the HMM is given by the dashed white curves. Before ANC, the HMM erroneously tracks the 60 Hz interference line. After ANC, the HMM successfully tracks the underlying GW signal.}}{14}{figure.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{frequency tracking before and after_real_Date}{{11}{14}{Same as Figure \ref {frequency tracking before and after1}, but for a GW signal (orange curve) injected into real LIGO noise. The $60 \, {\rm Hz}$ line is visible as a vertical yellow band in the left panel; it cannot be discerned in the right panel. The signal recovered by the HMM is given by the dashed white curves. Before ANC, the HMM erroneously tracks the 60 Hz interference line. After ANC, the HMM successfully tracks the underlying GW signal}{figure.11}{}}
